.TH fleetring-orphan 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-orphan \- Lists and removes orphans: copies the control plane doesn\*(Aqt know
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring orphan\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists and removes orphans: copies the control plane doesn\*(Aqt know
.PP
An orphan is a copy a data node keeps, closed, because the control plane didn\*(Aqt know its database, or held it only at a lower epoch, and the node saw no drop (ADR\-0042).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-orphan\-list(1)
Lists the orphans each data node keeps, or one node\*(Aqs
.TP
fleetring\-orphan\-remove(1)
Deletes a data node\*(Aqs orphan copy of a database, for good
